# 000-DRV-0080 — `audio_gw`: of several USB audio devices, the one set up last plays — done

**Type:** driver (`audio_gw`) · **Owner:** `DRV` · **Priority:** P2 · **Status:** done (2026-11-21) · **Blocked by:** — · **Roadmap:** A · **Constitution:** MC-6.1, MC-12.1, MC-12.3

## Problem

`audio_gw` took the first USB audio function `usb_host` had, and looked for no other while that one was attached (000-DRV-0073).

**The DEXP has USB audio of its own:** 0573:1573 on its xHCI's port 6 (its HD Audio has no codec). It is set up at every boot and never goes. So a speakerphone plugged in beside it was never used. 000-DRV-0073's "a USB device plugged in later becomes available without a restart" did not hold on such a machine.

## Plan

- **A look for newer devices.** With no stream running, every 2 s the gateway claims the audio interfaces that are not its own yet. Those belong to devices `usb_host` set up since the last look.
- **The one set up last is used.** Each usable device found takes the place of the one in use, the earliest set up first. This is what a headset plugged into a machine with sound of its own is expected to do.
- **The device replaced waits,** its interfaces kept (two devices at most). When the one in use goes, the latest of those waiting that still answers comes back. With none, the codec comes back as before.
- **A running stream is never moved.** The change happens only between streams.

**Not done here (MC-12.3):**
- **At boot** the order is `usb_host`'s set-up order (root ports, then hub ports), not the owner's choice. On the DEXP a speakerphone in a root port before port 6 is set up first, and 0573:1573 plays.
- **A choice the owner makes and the machine keeps** belongs to the audio interface (`idl/audio.wit`), in a new version of it.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] QEMU (`--suites usbaudio`): a second `usb-audio` plugged in beside the first is attached and the first waits; `beep` then reaches the second one's wav (0.86 s of tone); unplugged, the first is in use again; with the first unplugged too, the codec comes back.
- [x] On the DEXP: the speakerphone plugged in plays in place of 0573:1573, and with it unplugged 0573:1573 plays again. Release 202611210533, 2026-11-21, the speakerphone in the hub:
  ```
  779.338 usb_host: [USB] CAFE:4014 ON PORT 3.2 (FULL SPEED)
  779.554 audio_gw: [AUDIO] USB CAFE:4014 ATTACHED: PLAYBACK YES (INTERFACE 1, 2 CHANNELS, ENDPOINT 01, 196 BYTES, FEEDBACK), CAPTURE YES (INTERFACE 2, 1 CHANNELS, ENDPOINT 81, 98 BYTES)
  779.555 audio_gw: [AUDIO] USB 0573:1573 WAITS: A DEVICE SET UP AFTER IT IS USED
  …
  2144.799 audio_gw: [AUDIO] USB CAFE:4014 GONE (NotFound): 7001 PACKETS PLAYED, 1000 OF THEM SILENCE
  2144.799 audio_gw: [AUDIO] USB 0573:1573 AGAIN: THE DEVICE SET UP AFTER IT WENT
  ```
  - The maintainer heard the notes from the speakerphone while it was plugged in, and from the DEXP's own output after it was unplugged (a 2 s tone, then three notes).
  - He plugged it in and out several times before: each time it was taken, and 0573:1573 came back when it went.

## Resolution

Done on 2026-11-21 in `audio_gw/src/usbaudio.rs` (`take_newer`, `read`, `wait`, `fall_back`, `check`) and `audio_gw/src/main.rs` (the levels said again when the device in use changes); the `usbaudio` suite plugs a second device in and out.

It holds for the DEXP with its own 0573:1573 and the STM-Speaker (MC-12.1). What the plan left out stays out: the order at boot is `usb_host`'s, and the owner's kept choice waits for the audio interface.

**Seen on the way and fixed here:** the line of a device that went printed the counts of the last stream, which was another device's.

